 first-person weapon and the original status bar.","https://mrdoob.github.io/three-quake/",[294],[1360],{"_51":95,"_26":96},[1362],{"_51":1363,"_26":1364,"_207":1365},"Read the author’s AI and original-game credits","https://github.com/mrdoob/three-quake#credits","The maintainer distinguishes id Software’s original game from the Three.js port made with Claude assistance.",[1367],{"_51":1368,"_26":1369,"_207":1370},"Open the complete browser port","https://github.com/mrdoob/three-quake","Complete browser port, maps, runtime source and tests, with the shareware pak0.pak. Code is GPL-2.0; original Quake game data has separate terms and is not relicensed by the code license.",[1372],{"_51":1373,"_26":1357,"_207":1374},"Play Three Quake","Keyboard, mouse and a WebGL-capable browser. The included shareware data covers Episode 1; full-game content is separate.",[1376],{"_51":1377,"_26":1378,"_207":-7},"Read the port credits and creator dev log","https://github.com/mrdoob/three-quake#dev-log",[1380,1381,1382,1383],"Open the browser build, start a new single-player game and test the movement and firing controls.","Read the creator’s port credits and dev log alongside the original id Software source reference.","Inspect the browser renderer, game runtime, maps and tests to trace how the existing game was adapted.","Use the included shareware data for Episode 1; a registered full-game data set is separate and must be supplied by its owner.","Mr.doob credits Claude for assistance with the Three.js port. Quake’s game design and original implementation belong to id Software; this is an AI-assisted port, not a claim that AI created Quake. The README links a creator dev log without identifying a particular Claude client.",[1380,1381,1382,1383],{"_51":1377,"_26":1378,"_18":227},{"_51":1373,"_26":1357,"_18":307,"_207":1374},{"_51":1368,"_26":1369,"_207":1370,"_259":260},{"_51":1363,"_26":1364,"_207":1365},[117],"example:crown-defender-codex","crown-defender-codex","Crown Defender TD 3D · Codex build","Control a hero under an isometric camera, defend a castle through thirty waves and choose upgrades to unlock a cosmetic crown.","/examples/crown-defender-codex/",{"_20":1392,"_22":1393,"_24":1394,"_107":322,"_89":112,"_246":601,"_243":1448,"_9":1449,"_228":1450,"_19":1451,"_33":1452,"_204":1453,"_197":1454},[1398,1399,1400,1401,1402,1403,1404,1405,1406,1407,1408,1409,1410,1411,1412,1413,1414,1415,1416],{"_49":22,"_53":1393,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":1394,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":322,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":88,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":600,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":1448,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":1443,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":1440,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":812,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":225,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":1435,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":217,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":1431,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":1426,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":1423,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":1422},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":1418,"_72":1419,"_82":1420,"_33":1421,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":189},{"_49":50,"_55":177,"_51":178,"_53":1417},"2026-10-20T02:13:29.138Z","The complete source served locally: opening wave, hero and castle HUD.","/GameMap/media/learning/crown-defender-codex.webp","A hero defends a castle in Crown Defender’s isometric arena.","https://github.com/Aleksandr-Litvinenko/Codex.-Crown-Defender-TD-3D-browser-tower-defense-game",[1285],[1424,1425],{"_51":1292,"_26":1293},{"_51":95,"_26":96},[1427],{"_51":1428,"_26":1429,"_207":1430},"Read the author’s agent attribution","https://github.com/Aleksandr-Litvinenko/Codex.-Crown-Defender-TD-3D-browser-tower-defense-game/blob/main/COMPARISON.md","Author-published Russian comparison explicitly states that Codex built this version from the same requirements as the Claude Code project; no raw session is published.",[1432],{"_51":1433,"_26":1421,"_207":1434},"Open the complete Codex game project","Includes game.js, interface, bundled Three.js, runtime textures, requirements and optional WebSocket relay. No build or dependency installation for solo play. MIT code; see ASSET_CREDITS.md.",[1436],{"_51":1437,"_26":1438,"_207":1439},"Download and run Crown Defender","https://github.com/Aleksandr-Litvinenko/Codex.-Crown-Defender-TD-3D-browser-tower-defense-game/archive/refs/heads/main.zip","Static browser game. Run python3 -m http.server 8010 and open localhost:8010/index.html; choose Играть (Play). Russian interface. WASD/arrows move; semicolon attacks. Mobile joystick/buttons included. Optional two-player mode requires node server/multiplayer-server.mjs.",[1441],{"_51":1442,"_26":1429,"_207":-7},"Read the same-brief agent comparison",[1444,1445,1446,1447],"Serve the project locally and enter TD Defense.","Read the original requirements and same-brief comparison.","Inspect hero movement, wave progression and upgrade logic.","Change one upgrade and test losing, retrying and saved progress.","Aleksandr-Litvinenko attributes this build to Codex and publishes a comparison with a Claude Code version made from the same brief. The author states that the comparison concerns the agents’ original implementation choices, with assets and runtime code included here.",[1444,1445,1446,1447],{"_51":1442,"_26":1429,"_18":831},{"_51":1437,"_26":1438,"_18":217,"_207":1439},{"_51":1433,"_26":1421,"_259":260,"_207":1434},{"_51":1428,"_26":1429,"_207":1430},[1325,117],"example:magic-carpet-wizard-astra","magic-carpet-wizard-astra","Magic Carpet Wizard · A Thousand Skies","Fly a carpet over a tiny spherical world, thread scoring rings, cast three spells and face roaming enemies and bosses. Local ghost races let two players take turns.","/examples/magic-carpet-wizard-astra/",{"_20":1456,"_22":1457,"_24":1458,"_107":322,"_89":112,"_246":251,"_243":1510,"_9":1511,"_228":1512,"_19":1513,"_33":1514,"_204":1515,"_197":1516},[1462,1463,1464,1465,1466,1467,1468,1469,1470,1471,1472,1473,1474,1475,1476,1477,1478,1479,1480],{"_49":22,"_53":1457,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":1458,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":322,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":88,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":245,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":1510,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":1505,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":1502,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":227,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":312,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":1498,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":307,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":1494,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":1489,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":1487,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":1486},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":1482,"_72":1483,"_82":1484,"_33":1485,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":291},{"_49":50,"_55":177,"_51":178,"_53":1481},"2026-10-20T02:13:14.034Z","Capture from the creator’s playable flight game.","/GameMap/media/learning/magic-carpet-wizard-astra.webp","A carpet rider flies over a curved city toward a glowing ring.","https://threapchills.github.io/MagicCarpetWizard/",[439],[1488],{"_51":95,"_26":96},[1490],{"_51":1491,"_26":1492,"_207":1493},"See the creator’s Astra attribution","https://github.com/threapchills/MagicCarpetWizard","The author-controlled repository description names GPT-6 Astra. It does not establish which coding-agent client was used or publish the initial session.",[1495],{"_51":1496,"_26":1492,"_207":1497},"Open the complete carpet-flight project","Flight, enemies, spells, procedural world, audio, races and tests. Node.js 22; npm ci then npm run dev. No API keys; optional Google Fonts fall back to system fonts.",[1499],{"_51":1500,"_26":1485,"_207":1501},"Play Magic Carpet Wizard","Desktop WebGL2, mouse and keyboard. Enter starts; WASD steers/climbs, mouse plus left click aims/casts, 1–3 changes spells, Space rolls, Shift boosts, and R retries.",[1503],{"_51":1504,"_26":1492,"_207":-7},"Read the creator’s implementation guide",[1506,1507,1508,1509],"Play an adventure run and test flight and spells.","Read the creator’s attribution and audio notes.","Inspect flight rules, collision and rendering modules.","Adjust one obstacle or spell and test a retry and ghost race.","The creator’s repository About section attributes the game to GPT-6 Astra. The README documents original procedural geometry and textures plus supplied audio; it does not publish prompts, a transcript or an exact division of human and model work.",[1506,1507,1508,1509],{"_51":1504,"_26":1492,"_18":227},{"_51":1500,"_26":1485,"_18":307,"_207":1501},{"_51":1496,"_26":1492,"_259":260,"_207":1497},{"_51":1491,"_26":1492,"_207":1493},[117],"example:sakura-crossing-qwen","3D Sakura Crossing: an exploration prototype","Explore a cel-shaded Japanese neighbourhood with a working railway crossing, residents, a lifting bridge, a drivable car, and a swimmable river.",{"_20":113,"_22":1518,"_24":1519,"_107":322,"_89":112,"_246":251,"_243":1574,"_9":1575,"_228":1576,"_19":1577,"_33":1578,"_204":1579,"_197":1580},[1522,1523,1524,1525,1526,1527,1528,1529,1530,1531,1532,1533,1534,1535,1536,1537,1538,1539,1540,1541],{"_49":22,"_53":1518,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":1519,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":322,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":88,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":245,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":1574,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":1569,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":1565,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":812,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":312,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":1560,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":307,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":1557,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":1552,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":1550,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":1549},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":1545,"_72":1546,"_82":1547,"_33":1548,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":367},{"_49":50,"_55":361,"_51":362,"_53":1353},{"_49":59,"_55":356,"_51":357,"_61":1542},[1543],{"_51":357,"_26":1544},"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/danymaniglie-cmyk/3d-sakura-crossing/main/docs/anteprima.gif","Creator-published gameplay animation from the repository README.","/GameMap/media/learning/sakura-crossing-qwen.webp","Sakura Crossing gameplay in a cel-shaded Japanese neighbourhood at dusk.","https://github.com/danymaniglie-cmyk/3d-sakura-crossing",[510],[1551],{"_51":95,"_26":96},[1553],{"_51":1554,"_26":1555,"_207":1556},"Read the Qwen and human contribution credit","https://github.com/danymaniglie-cmyk/3d-sakura-crossing#credits","README explicitly distinguishes locally generated Qwen code from human review, debugging, and extensions. The creator’s linked Reddit build account identifies Claude Code CLI as the harness, not the Claude model.",[1558],{"_51":449,"_26":1548,"_207":1559},"GPL-3.0 source with complete index.html, vendored Three.js, procedural textures, and implementation notes. Run python3 -m http.server 5191 and open localhost:5191/index.html; file:// loading is unsupported. The original author has ended active development. The creator describes an exploration prototype, not a finished campaign; no complete win/loss loop is claimed.",[1561],{"_51":1562,"_26":1563,"_207":1564},"Explore Sakura Crossing","https://danymaniglie-cmyk.github.io/3d-sakura-crossing/","Exploration prototype. WASD walks, Shift runs, mouse drag looks, E talks, F enters/exits the car, and Space/C swims up/down. Touch controls included; mobile performance remains limited.",[1566],{"_51":1567,"_26":1568,"_207":-7},"Read the rendering and implementation recipe","https://github.com/danymaniglie-cmyk/3d-sakura-crossing/blob/main/CARTOON.md",[1570,1571,1572,1573],"Explore the browser world on foot, then try the car, river, and moving bridge.","Read the credits and the author’s account of using a local Qwen model through Claude Code CLI.","Inspect CARTOON.md and the complete index.html plus vendored Three.js dependency.","Serve a local copy over HTTP, change one interaction, and verify movement and collisions.","The repository credits code generation to locally running Qwen 3.8 27B, followed by human review, debugging, and extensions. In the linked build account the author identifies Claude Code CLI as the harness with Qwen as its model.",[1570,1571,1572,1573],{"_51":1567,"_26":1568,"_18":831},{"_51":1562,"_26":1563,"_18":307,"_207":1564},{"_51":449,"_26":1548,"_259":260,"_207":1559},{"_51":1554,"_26":1555,"_207":1556},[117],"example:sprout-quest-claude","sprout-quest-claude","Sprout Quest","Explore a small world, fight real-time arena battles, gather materials, craft gear and rebuild a village. Sprout Quest is a mobile-first adventure with a 2D world and live-rendered 3D characters and items.","/examples/sprout-quest-claude/",{"_20":1582,"_22":1583,"_24":1584,"_107":1645,"_1106":1646,"_89":250,"_246":601,"_243":1643,"_9":1647,"_228":1648,"_19":1649,"_33":1650,"_204":1651,"_197":1652},[1588,1589,1590,1591,1592,1593,1594,1595,1596,1597,1598,1599,1600,1601,1602,1603,1604,1605,1606,1607,1608],{"_49":22,"_53":1583,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":1584,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":1645,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":1103,"_234":1104,"_61":1644,"_55":1106,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":247,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":600,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":1643,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":1638,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":1635,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":812,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":312,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":1630,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":307,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":1626,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":1621,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":1617,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":1616},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":1612,"_72":1613,"_82":1614,"_33":1615,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":367},{"_49":50,"_55":361,"_51":362,"_53":1353},{"_49":59,"_55":356,"_51":357,"_61":1609},[1610],{"_51":357,"_26":1611},"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aibengineering/sprout-quest/main/docs/teaser.webp","A combat frame from the creator’s portrait gameplay animation, fitted without cropping.","/GameMap/media/learning/sprout-quest-claude.webp","A small sword-wielding adventurer fights creatures on a forest path, with a portrait mobile touch joystick.","https://github.com/aibengineering/sprout-quest#readme",[510],[1618,1619,1620],{"_51":510,"_26":511},{"_51":95,"_26":96},{"_51":1078,"_26":1079},[1622],{"_51":1623,"_26":1624,"_207":1625},"Read the creator’s AI attribution","https://github.com/aibengineering/sprout-quest#how-it-was-built","README separates the original build from later human playtest/AI iteration; publishes source modules, generated models and runtime assets, plus a prompt summary. Source-checked; full reproduction not performed.",[1627],{"_51":880,"_26":1628,"_207":1629},"https://github.com/aibengineering/sprout-quest","Complete game code, runtime GLBs/sprite atlases, Blender scripts and tests. bun install then bun run dev opens localhost:3000; normal builds use committed art and do not require Blender. No root LICENSE was found, so public source visibility does not establish broad reuse permission.",[1631],{"_51":1632,"_26":1633,"_207":1634},"Play Sprout Quest","https://aibengineering.github.io/sprout-quest/","Author-hosted browser adventure designed for portrait phones, with desktop keyboard controls and localStorage saves.",[1636],{"_51":1637,"_26":1624,"_207":-7},"Read the creator’s build account",[1639,1640,1641,1642],"Play the portrait-browser prologue and follow its first fight, gathering and forge tasks.","Read the build account to see how human phone playtests guided later Claude Code changes.","Run bun install and bun run dev; inspect the game modules, committed runtime assets and Blender builders.","Change one combat, crafting or story rule with an agent, then replay the affected progression and save flow.","The creator says Claude Code generated the game, tests and Blender art pipeline from plain-language requests while the human played on a phone and gave feedback. The repository contains the runtime art as well as its source builders.",[1078],"Custom Canvas 2D + Three.js · TypeScript",[1078],[1639,1640,1641,1642],{"_51":1637,"_26":1624,"_18":831},{"_51":1632,"_26":1633,"_18":307,"_207":1634},{"_51":880,"_26":1628,"_207":1629,"_259":260},{"_51":1623,"_26":1624,"_207":1625},[541,117,1116],"example:astra-floor-ai","astra-floor-ai","Astra Floor","Fight six zombie waves and a final boss in a first-person industrial arena, managing ammunition, recoil, stamina and purchases between rounds.","/examples/astra-floor-ai/",{"_20":1654,"_22":1655,"_24":1656,"_107":1714,"_89":112,"_246":251,"_243":1713,"_9":1715,"_228":1716,"_19":1717,"_33":1718,"_204":1719,"_197":1720},[1660,1661,1662,1663,1664,1665,1666,1667,1668,1669,1670,1671,1672,1673,1674,1675,1676,1677,1678,1679],{"_49":22,"_53":1655,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":1656,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":1714,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":88,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":245,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":1713,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":1708,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":1705,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":227,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":312,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":1700,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":307,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":1695,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":1691,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":1689,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":1687},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":1683,"_72":1684,"_82":1685,"_33":1686,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":367},{"_49":50,"_55":361,"_51":362,"_53":1353},{"_49":59,"_55":356,"_51":357,"_61":1680},[1681],{"_51":357,"_26":1682},"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/35972360-9042-401a-9545-e94769da294e","The creator’s rifle-combat screenshot.","/GameMap/media/learning/astra-floor-ai.webp","Astra Floor rifle combat against a zombie wave, with health, ammunition and wave counters.","https://github.com/MartinDelophy/awesome-gpt-6-astra/issues/96",[1688,938],"ChatGPT",[1690],{"_51":95,"_26":96},[1692],{"_51":1693,"_26":1686,"_207":1694},"Read the author’s division of AI work","The repository owner’s submission distinguishes Astra from Antigravity work. The README also credits both tools; no full conversation archive is supplied.",[1696],{"_51":1697,"_26":1698,"_207":1699},"Open the complete FPS project","https://github.com/BEROCHLU/astrafloor","Game implementation, procedural models, bundled textures/music and tests. Node.js 22.13+; npm install then npm run dev. Third-party texture credits are documented separately.",[1701],{"_51":1702,"_26":1703,"_207":1704},"Play Astra Floor","https://astrafloor.berochlu.workers.dev/","Desktop WebGL, keyboard and mouse. Wait for INITIALIZING to finish, choose a difficulty, then DEPLOY. WASD moves, mouse aims/fires, R reloads, Q heals, G throws a grenade, and V uses melee. Runs are not saved. The in-app browser could not capture the mouse during review; a normal desktop browser is recommended.",[1706],{"_51":1707,"_26":1686,"_207":-7},"Read the creator’s AI development disclosure",[1709,1710,1711,1712],"Choose Normal difficulty and enter the first wave.","Read the creator’s architecture and model disclosure.","Inspect procedural weapons, enemies and audio implementation.","Tune one weapon or enemy and verify a wave and shop transition.","BEROCHLU credits GPT-6 Astra with much of the architecture, procedural 3D generation and Web Audio synthesis. Antigravity 2.0 supplied other implementation and iterative refinement. The disclosure does not claim a single-prompt build.","Three.js · TypeScript (React UI)",[1709,1710,1711,1712],{"_51":1707,"_26":1686,"_18":227},{"_51":1702,"_26":1703,"_18":307,"_207":1704},{"_51":1697,"_26":1698,"_259":260,"_207":1699},{"_51":1693,"_26":1686,"_207":1694},[117],"example:rhythm-master-windsurf","rhythm-master-windsurf","Rhythm Master 3D","A four-lane music game with generated synth tracks, difficulty settings, combos and a special mode, implemented as a single browser HTML file.","/examples/rhythm-master-windsurf/",{"_20":1722,"_22":1723,"_24":1724,"_107":1778,"_89":112,"_243":1777,"_9":1779,"_228":1780,"_19":1781,"_33":1782,"_204":1783,"_197":1784,"_246":251},[1728,1729,1730,1731,1732,1733,1734,1735,1736,1737,1738,1739,1740,1741,1742,1743,1744,1745,1746],{"_49":22,"_53":1723,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":1724,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":1778,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":88,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":245,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":1777,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":1772,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":1769,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":812,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":225,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":1764,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":217,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":1760,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":1755,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":1753,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":1751},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":1747,"_72":1748,"_82":1749,"_33":1750,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":189},{"_49":50,"_55":177,"_51":178,"_53":1353},"The unmodified public HTML game after track start and a normal note-key input.","/GameMap/media/learning/rhythm-master-windsurf.webp","A purple 3D rhythm highway with four note lanes, score and combo panels, a track timer and keyboard prompts.","https://github.com/frankjniu/rhythm-game",[1752,294],"Windsurf",[1754],{"_51":95,"_26":96},[1756],{"_51":1757,"_26":1758,"_207":1759},"Read the author’s AI tools and prompt disclosure","https://www.linkedin.com/posts/frankniu_if-youre-not-vibe-coding-with-claude-sonnet-activity-7304977951761039362-2xQe","The creator identifies Claude Sonnet 3.7, describes passing output into Windsurf, and links the exact rhythm-game repository in the same post.",[1761],{"_51":1762,"_26":1750,"_207":1763},"Open the complete rhythm-game source","The full game is rhythm.html, with procedural music and geometry rather than a separate asset download. Third-party libraries load from CDNs. No repository code license is declared.",[1765],{"_51":1766,"_26":1767,"_207":1768},"Download and run Rhythm Master 3D","https://github.com/frankjniu/rhythm-game/archive/refs/heads/main.zip","No public hosted build was verified. Serve the downloaded directory and open rhythm.html. External CDNs supply Three.js and Tone.js, so internet access is needed; a click starts audio.",[1770],{"_51":1771,"_26":1758,"_207":-7},"Read the creator’s build workflow",[1773,1774,1775,1776],"Download the repository and serve its directory with a local HTTP server, then open rhythm.html.","Choose a track and difficulty, start the game, and use D/F/J/K as notes reach the target zone.","Test combo scoring, Escape pause and the Space special mode before changing timing or difficulty.","Compare the single-file implementation with the creator’s original brief and debugging workflow.","Frank Niu links this game from a creator post describing a Claude Sonnet 3.7 web-chat-to-Windsurf workflow: generate an initial game, diagnose issues in chat, then apply changes in Windsurf. It is a human-steered coding example, not evidence that Claude Code or a single autonomous run built it.","Three.js · Tone.js · JavaScript",[1773,1774,1775,1776],{"_51":1771,"_26":1758,"_18":831},{"_51":1766,"_26":1767,"_18":217,"_207":1768},{"_51":1762,"_26":1750,"_207":1763,"_259":260},{"_51":1757,"_26":1758,"_207":1759},[117],"example:golden-hour-skatepark-cursor","golden-hour-skatepark-cursor","Golden Hour Skatepark","Skate an original beachside park: carve transitions, ollie, flip, grind, manual, bail and recover. This complete third-person sandbox has transient trick combos and a changeable time of day, with no levels or persistent score.","/examples/golden-hour-skatepark-cursor/",{"_20":1786,"_22":1787,"_24":1788,"_107":1851,"_1106":1852,"_89":112,"_246":251,"_243":1849,"_9":1853,"_228":1854,"_19":1855,"_33":1856,"_204":1857,"_197":1858},[1792,1793,1794,1795,1796,1797,1798,1799,1800,1801,1802,1803,1804,1805,1806,1807,1808,1809,1810,1811,1812],{"_49":22,"_53":1787,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":1788,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":1851,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":1103,"_234":1104,"_61":1850,"_55":1106,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":88,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":245,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":1849,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":1844,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":1840,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":812,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":312,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":1835,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":307,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":1830,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":1825,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":1822,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":1820},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":1816,"_72":1817,"_82":1818,"_33":1819,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":367},{"_49":50,"_55":361,"_51":362,"_53":1353},{"_49":59,"_55":356,"_51":357,"_61":1813},[1814],{"_51":357,"_26":1815},"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/StarKnightt/skate-park/main/docs/media/02-half-pipe-air.jpg","The creator’s actual half-pipe gameplay frame, with the skater and the procedural park.","/GameMap/media/learning/golden-hour-skatepark-cursor.webp","A skater is airborne above a half-pipe in a palm-lined skatepark under a warm evening sky.","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park#readme",[1821],"Cursor",[1823,1824],{"_51":95,"_26":96},{"_51":1078,"_26":1079},[1826],{"_51":1827,"_26":1828,"_207":1829},"Read the creator’s Cursor contribution account","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park#how-it-was-built","The README explicitly names Cursor AI agents and separates builder passes, critic feedback and human playtests; docs/MAKING-OF.md provides a detailed account. Source-checked; performance and playability claims were not reproduced.",[1831],{"_51":1832,"_26":1833,"_207":1834},"Open the complete skating project","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park","Complete TypeScript game, procedural park code, runtime skater/crowd GLBs, textures, audio and source tools. CI uses Node 22 and pnpm 10.18.0; pnpm install then pnpm dev at 127.0.0.1:5188. Ports are fixed. No root LICENSE was found; CC0 media, Mixamo animations and dependencies keep separate terms.",[1836],{"_51":1837,"_26":1838,"_207":1839},"Play Golden Hour Skatepark","https://starknightt.github.io/skate-park/","Browser skating sandbox with keyboard, optional mouse/gamepad and touch controls. Press any key, click or tap to take over from the title-screen rider. Phone testing reported by the creator used desktop emulation; Firefox and desktop Safari remain untested.",[1841],{"_51":1842,"_26":1843,"_207":-7},"Read the builder-and-critic development account","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park/blob/main/docs/MAKING-OF.md",[1845,1846,1847,1848],"Play the park and test pushing, carving, one trick, a bail and recovery.","Read the making-of account and separate human feedback, agent implementation and third-party assets.","Use Node 22 with pnpm 10.18.0, then pnpm install and pnpm dev; inspect the collision mesh and character pipeline.","Ask an agent to adjust one movement or camera parameter, then compare transition riding, tricks and recovery across the park.","The author says Cursor AI agents implemented the game through builder and visual-critic passes, with human playtests refining controls. Code-built environments and procedural riding are combined with Cursor-generated artwork, credited CC0 audio/textures and Mixamo recovery animations.",[1078],"Three.js · TypeScript",[1078],[1845,1846,1847,1848],{"_51":1842,"_26":1843,"_18":831},{"_51":1837,"_26":1838,"_18":307,"_207":1839},{"_51":1832,"_26":1833,"_259":260,"_207":1834},{"_51":1827,"_26":1828,"_207":1829},[117,1116],"example:surge-for-oinja-codex","surge-for-oinja-codex","SURGE for Oinja","Shape an electrical build while surviving mechanical swarms across two interactive maps. Automatic attacks leave movement, dodging, upgrades and facility restoration to the player.","/examples/surge-for-oinja-codex/",{"_20":1860,"_22":1861,"_24":1862,"_107":1920,"_89":112,"_246":251,"_243":1919,"_9":1921,"_228":1922,"_19":1923,"_33":1924,"_204":1925,"_197":1926},[1866,1867,1868,1869,1870,1871,1872,1873,1874,1875,1876,1877,1878,1879,1880,1881,1882,1883,1884,1885],{"_49":22,"_53":1861,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":1862,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":1920,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":88,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":245,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":1919,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":1914,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":1911,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":227,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":312,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":1906,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":307,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":1901,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":1897,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":1894,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":1893},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":1889,"_72":1890,"_82":1891,"_33":1892,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":367},{"_49":50,"_55":361,"_51":362,"_53":1353},{"_49":59,"_55":356,"_51":357,"_61":1886},[1887],{"_51":357,"_26":1888},"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8adca12c-6ede-46b3-96e7-128de3709de6","The creator’s Tidal Observatory gameplay screenshot.","/GameMap/media/learning/surge-for-oinja-codex.webp","SURGE gameplay in the Tidal Observatory with a character, support machine, enemies and combat HUD.","https://github.com/MartinDelophy/awesome-gpt-6-astra/issues/106",[1285],[1895,1896],{"_51":1292,"_26":1293},{"_51":95,"_26":96},[1898],{"_51":1899,"_26":1892,"_207":1900},"Read the creator’s Codex contribution statement","Submitted by Olivia295, the source repository owner, with explicit human and model responsibilities; not a complete session transcript.",[1902],{"_51":1903,"_26":1904,"_207":1905},"Open the complete survival-game project","https://github.com/Olivia295/SURGE-for-Oinja","Includes gameplay, physics, models, assets, translations and tests. Requires Node.js 22; run npm ci and npm run dev. No application server or API key is required.",[1907],{"_51":1908,"_26":1909,"_207":1910},"Play SURGE for Oinja","https://oinja-game.vercel.app/","Desktop WebGL and keyboard. WASD/arrows move, Space dodges, Q releases Sync Burst, and E interacts. Attacks are automatic. English and Chinese; no mobile touch controls.",[1912],{"_51":1913,"_26":1892,"_207":-7},"Read the creator’s development account",[1915,1916,1917,1918],"Start a run and try movement, dodging and automatic attacks.","Read the creator’s contribution disclosure.","Inspect combat, progression and map code under src/surge/.","Change one ability combination and check its effect during a new run.","Olivia used GPT-6 Astra in Codex for combat, ability synergies, procedural environments, interface and debugging. The original Oinja universe, creative direction and playtest feedback came from the creator; development involved repeated sessions and revisions.","Three.js · Rapier 3D · TypeScript",[1915,1916,1917,1918],{"_51":1913,"_26":1892,"_18":227},{"_51":1908,"_26":1909,"_18":307,"_207":1910},{"_51":1903,"_26":1904,"_259":260,"_207":1905},{"_51":1899,"_26":1892,"_207":1900},[1325,117],"example:project-plateau","project-plateau","Project Plateau: Proof Before Dark","A first-person field-photography expedition inspired by The Lost World: frame prehistoric animals, manage four photographic plates, avoid threats and return to camp before daylight fades.","/examples/project-plateau/",{"_20":1928,"_22":1929,"_24":1930,"_107":1990,"_1106":1991,"_89":112,"_243":1988,"_9":1992,"_228":1993,"_19":1994,"_33":1995,"_204":1996,"_197":1997,"_246":251},[1934,1935,1936,1937,1938,1939,1940,1941,1942,1943,1944,1945,1946,1947,1948,1949,1950,1951,1952,1953,1954],{"_49":22,"_53":1929,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":1930,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":1990,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":1103,"_234":1104,"_61":1989,"_55":1106,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":88,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":245,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":1988,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":1983,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":1980,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":812,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":312,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":1975,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":307,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":1970,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":1965,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":1963,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":1962},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":1958,"_72":1959,"_82":1960,"_33":1961,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":367},{"_49":50,"_55":361,"_51":362,"_53":1353},{"_49":59,"_55":356,"_51":357,"_61":1955},[1956],{"_51":357,"_26":1957},"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zenstory-ai/novel-to-game/7758caa8d9578f19780349e7b4e4115ef831fd7a/examples/project-plateau/build/evidence/current-run/01-field-glade.jpg","A creator-published frame from the recorded expedition, showing the field camera, animal family and remaining daylight.","/GameMap/media/learning/project-plateau.webp","The player’s field camera points toward a prehistoric animal family beside a brook, with photographic plate and daylight indicators.","https://github.com/zenstory-ai/novel-to-game/blob/7758caa8d9578f19780349e7b4e4115ef831fd7a/examples/project-plateau/build/evidence/current-run/01-field-glade.jpg",[439],[1964],{"_51":95,"_26":96},[1966],{"_51":1967,"_26":1968,"_207":1969},"Read the creator’s adaptation and QA account","https://github.com/zenstory-ai/novel-to-game#what-the-qa-record-admits-it-did-not-test","The author explains the recorded camera-to-result-and-restart route and its limits; GameMap is not claiming to have reproduced that complete route.",[1971],{"_51":1972,"_26":1973,"_207":1974},"Open the full expedition project","https://github.com/zenstory-ai/novel-to-game/tree/main/examples/project-plateau","Three.js/Vite game with local runtime models, textures, sound, source adaptation documents and QA inputs. Requires Node 22.12+ for local tooling. Blender scripts are asset-production sources, not required for normal play.",[1976],{"_51":1977,"_26":1978,"_207":1979},"Play Project Plateau","https://plateau.vibecoco.ai/","Desktop landscape browser with WebGL2, keyboard and mouse. Mobile devices may show the creator’s short recorded preview instead of the full game.",[1981],{"_51":1982,"_26":1973,"_207":-7},"Read the expedition build and design workspace",[1984,1985,1986,1987],"Start the desktop expedition and learn movement, camera, crouching and return-to-camp controls.","Compare how subject framing, cover and photographic plates create choices from the novel’s expedition premise.","Read the build brief and verification record to separate a tested route from untested device, sound and optional encounter behavior.","For local play, enter examples/project-plateau/build/app, use Node 22.12+ to install dependencies, then run npm start; the committed runtime assets do not require Blender regeneration.","The creator presents Project Plateau as a NovelToGame adaptation built through analysis, concept, world design, art direction, implementation and QA stages. The public workspace includes game code, committed models and textures, asset-generation scripts and the input trace for one tested path; its coding client is not explicitly identified.",[1078],"Three.js · WebGL2",[1078],[1984,1985,1986,1987],{"_51":1982,"_26":1973,"_18":831},{"_51":1977,"_26":1978,"_18":307,"_207":1979},{"_51":1972,"_26":1973,"_207":1974,"_259":260},{"_51":1967,"_26":1968,"_207":1969},[117],"example:nagi-home-cowork","nagi-home-cowork","Nagi Home","Care for Nagi, a small crab living in a procedural home: place food, throw a ball, request furniture activities and follow a diary as daily needs change. It is a quiet life simulation with saved progress.","/examples/nagi-home-cowork/",{"_20":1999,"_22":2000,"_24":2001,"_107":2053,"_89":112,"_246":251,"_243":2052,"_9":2054,"_228":2055,"_19":2056,"_33":2057,"_204":2058,"_197":2059},[2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023],{"_49":22,"_53":2000,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":2001,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":2053,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":88,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":245,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":2052,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":2047,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":2044,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":227,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":312,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":2040,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":307,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":2036,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":2032,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":2030,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":2028},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":2024,"_72":2025,"_82":2026,"_33":2027,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":291},{"_49":50,"_55":177,"_51":178,"_53":1353},"The live Cowork-created simulation after placing food on the floor and throwing a ball.","/GameMap/media/learning/nagi-home-cowork.webp","Nagi the blue crab in a furnished three-dimensional home, with daily needs, food placement feedback and the ball activity.","https://tanuu5.github.io/nagi-home/",[2029],"Claude Cowork",[2031],{"_51":95,"_26":96},[2033],{"_51":1623,"_26":2034,"_207":2035},"https://github.com/tanuu5/nagi-home#readme","README credits explicitly name Claude Cowork and Claude Opus 5.5, with human planning/publishing attribution.",[2037],{"_51":880,"_26":2038,"_207":2039},"https://github.com/tanuu5/nagi-home","Complete single-file HTML with procedural Three.js scene, need/activity systems, dialogue and localStorage saves; MIT code. Three.js r169 is loaded from jsDelivr and fonts from Google Fonts, so a clean run requires those network resources. No coding-agent subscription is needed to play.",[2041],{"_51":2042,"_26":2027,"_207":2043},"Play Nagi Home","Japanese interface. Drag to orbit, wheel/pinch to zoom; the food and ball buttons trigger interactions. Normal food placement and ball throwing were checked in Chrome, including diary feedback. This is a life simulation without a combat or level-completion goal.",[2045],{"_51":2046,"_26":2034,"_207":-7},"Read the creator’s Cowork and simulation notes",[2048,2049,2050,2051],"Place food or throw the ball, then watch Nagi’s activity and diary change.","Read the single index.html to follow daily needs, activity selection, Three.js models and localStorage persistence.","Serve the repository with a static HTTP server or open its HTML in a browser; Three.js and fonts are fetched from external CDNs.","Change one need or activity rule, then check its effect at normal and accelerated time speeds.","The creator explicitly says Claude Opus 5.5 generated the code in Claude Cowork. Human planning and publishing are credited separately. Cowork is retained as the actual client rather than being relabelled Claude Code; the conversation itself is not published.","Three.js r169 · JavaScript",[2048,2049,2050,2051],{"_51":2046,"_26":2034,"_18":227},{"_51":2042,"_26":2027,"_18":307,"_207":2043},{"_51":880,"_26":2038,"_259":260,"_207":2039},{"_51":1623,"_26":2034,"_207":2035},[117],"example:fishslop-claude","fishslop-claude","Fishslop","Pilot a bathyscaphe through a sunken reef, feed fish, collect the coins they drop and buy new residents or submarine parts. Sonar briefly reveals an otherwise invisible Veilfin.","/examples/fishslop-claude/",{"_20":2061,"_22":2062,"_24":2063,"_107":2117,"_89":112,"_246":251,"_243":2116,"_9":2118,"_228":2119,"_19":2120,"_33":2121,"_204":2122,"_197":2123},[2067,2068,2069,2070,2071,2072,2073,2074,2075,2076,2077,2078,2079,2080,2081,2082,2083,2084,2085],{"_49":22,"_53":2062,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":2063,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":2117,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":88,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":245,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":2116,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":2111,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":2107,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":2106,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":312,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":2102,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":307,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":2098,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":2093,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":2091,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":2090},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":2086,"_72":2087,"_82":2088,"_33":2089,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":291},{"_49":50,"_55":177,"_51":178,"_53":1353},"The live reef after steering, feeding, coin feedback and sonar, using the low-quality preset.","/GameMap/media/learning/fishslop-claude.webp","A submarine in a three-dimensional reef with ruins, fish, feeding particles, coins and a recharging sonar display.","https://vasu-devs.github.io/FishSlop_Opus5.5/",[294],[2092],{"_51":95,"_26":96},[2094],{"_51":2095,"_26":2096,"_207":2097},"Read the initial AI-credited implementation","https://github.com/vasu-devs/FishSlop_Opus5.5/commit/e7a7a2dd61b6da92f9512ccabafad13e1e9a3df4","Initial game implementation explicitly credits Claude Opus 5.5 as co-author; later fix commits repeat that credit. A model credit alone is not attributed to Claude Code.",[2099],{"_51":880,"_26":2100,"_207":2101},"https://github.com/vasu-devs/FishSlop_Opus5.5","Complete simulation, Three.js renderer, procedural assets, UI, audio, lockfile and tests. npm ci then npm run dev; the README’s Node 20.19+ does not cover every Node 22 version supported by its current Vite 8 dependency, so use Node 22.12+ or another compatible current runtime. No licence file was found; source availability is not a general reuse grant.",[2103],{"_51":2104,"_26":2089,"_207":2105},"Play Fishslop","WebGL2 with keyboard, mouse or touch. WASD steers, E/Q changes depth, Space feeds, F pings sonar and B opens the dock. The low-quality preset ?quality=low&scale=0.5 was used to check steering, feeding, coin feedback and sonar.","quickstart",[2108],{"_51":2109,"_26":2110,"_207":-7},"Read the game rules and project structure","https://github.com/vasu-devs/FishSlop_Opus5.5#readme",[2112,2113,2114,2115],"Dive in, steer with WASD, hold Space to feed fish and use F for sonar.","Compare the renderer-free simulation, feeding economy and save parser with the Three.js scene.","Use a Vite-compatible Node runtime, npm ci and npm run dev; Node 22.12+ meets the current Vite 8 requirement.","Change one fish or upgrade value, then check food, dropped coins, dock purchases and saved progress.","The creator’s initial implementation and subsequent fixes explicitly credit Claude Opus 5.5 as a commit co-author. This is evidence of an AI-assisted development contribution; it does not identify the coding client or establish that all code was generated by the model. The reef, fish, textures and sounds are generated by game code.","Three.js · TypeScript · Web Audio",[2112,2113,2114,2115],{"_51":2109,"_26":2110,"_18":2106},{"_51":2104,"_26":2089,"_18":307,"_207":2105},{"_51":880,"_26":2100,"_259":260,"_207":2101},{"_51":2095,"_26":2096,"_207":2097},[117],"example:pelican-bike-claude","pelican-bike-claude","Pelican on a Bike","Ride a helmeted pelican along a procedural coast, change lanes to catch fish, jump and unlock small achievements. The complete Three.js project includes its own character, bicycle, ocean, audio and day/night systems.","/examples/pelican-bike-claude/",{"_20":2125,"_22":2126,"_24":2127,"_107":322,"_89":112,"_246":251,"_243":2178,"_9":2179,"_228":2180,"_19":2181,"_33":2182,"_204":2183,"_197":2184},[2131,2132,2133,2134,2135,2136,2137,2138,2139,2140,2141,2142,2143,2144,2145,2146,2147,2148,2149],{"_49":22,"_53":2126,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":2127,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":322,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":88,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":245,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":2178,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":2173,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":2170,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":387,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":312,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":2166,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":307,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":2162,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":2158,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":2155,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":2154},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":2150,"_72":2151,"_82":2152,"_33":2153,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":291},{"_49":50,"_55":177,"_51":178,"_53":1353},"The live coastal ride after acceleration, a first jump and a camera change.","/GameMap/media/learning/pelican-bike-claude.webp","A white pelican riding a bicycle along a three-dimensional coast, with speed, distance, fish and achievement HUD.","https://claude-opus-5-5.riba2534.cn/",[510],[2156,2157],{"_51":510,"_26":511},{"_51":95,"_26":96},[2159],{"_51":1623,"_26":2160,"_207":2161},"https://github.com/riba2534/claude-opus-5-5-demo#readme","Creator-published prompt and session summary, with exact Claude Code attribution. The model-led long-run tests described there were not repeated by GameMap.",[2163],{"_51":880,"_26":2164,"_207":2165},"https://github.com/riba2534/claude-opus-5-5-demo/tree/main/pelican-bike","Complete pelican-bike source, build script and procedural assets. Run npm install and node build.mjs in that subdirectory, then open dist/index.html. The repository contains three distinct games; this case selects only the pelican game. Package metadata names ISC, but no repository-wide licence text is supplied.",[2167],{"_51":2168,"_26":2153,"_207":2169},"Play Pelican on a Bike","Keyboard and touch controls; W/S accelerate/brake, A/D change lanes, Space jumps and C changes camera. A muted entry is available. Desktop launch, acceleration, jump achievement and camera change were checked.",[2171],{"_51":2172,"_26":2160,"_207":-7},"Read the original prompt and development account",[2174,2175,2176,2177],"Start a muted ride, accelerate with W/S, change lanes with A/D and jump with Space.","Compare the published one-sentence prompt with the pelican, bicycle, cloth, ocean and camera modules.","In pelican-bike, install dependencies and run node build.mjs; open the resulting dist/index.html in a browser.","Change one collection or cycling rule, then check movement, jump, score feedback and restart.","The creator reports generating the game with Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code from one Chinese sentence. The README publishes that prompt and describes model-led browser testing and later fixes; the no-manual-code claim is the creator’s, not a measured authorship audit.",[2174,2175,2176,2177],{"_51":2172,"_26":2160,"_18":387},{"_51":2168,"_26":2153,"_18":307,"_207":2169},{"_51":880,"_26":2164,"_259":260,"_207":2165},{"_51":1623,"_26":2160,"_207":2161},[541,117],"example:core-business-claude","core-business-claude","Core Business","Drill for minerals, manage fuel and hull condition, and spend earnings at surface shops in a non-commercial mining tech demo inspired by Motherload. Three.js renders the 2.5D world while Blender scripts produce its 3D assets.","/examples/core-business-claude/",{"_20":2186,"_22":2187,"_24":2188,"_107":322,"_89":112,"_246":251,"_243":2240,"_9":2243,"_228":2244,"_19":2245,"_33":2246,"_204":2247,"_197":2248,"_1106":2249},[2192,2193,2194,2195,2196,2197,2198,2199,2200,2201,2202,2203,2204,2205,2206,2207,2208,2209,2210,2211],{"_49":22,"_53":2187,"_55":22,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":2188,"_55":24,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":248,"_53":322,"_55":107,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":1103,"_234":1104,"_61":2241,"_55":1106,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":87,"_53":88,"_55":89,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":244,"_53":245,"_55":246,"_57":86},{"_49":50,"_51":241,"_53":2240,"_55":243,"_57":58},{"_49":190,"_51":233,"_234":235,"_61":2235,"_55":9,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":229,"_61":2232,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":226,"_53":812,"_55":228,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":224,"_53":312,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":218,"_61":2228,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":216,"_53":307,"_55":19,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":2224,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":209,"_53":210,"_55":33,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":202,"_61":2220,"_55":204,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":195,"_61":2217,"_55":197,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_55":191,"_51":192,"_61":2216},{"_49":180,"_55":115,"_51":2212,"_72":2213,"_82":2214,"_33":2215,"_185":186,"_187":188,"_56":291},{"_49":50,"_55":177,"_51":178,"_53":1353},"The running author-hosted mining tech demo, captured with the Metal rendering backend.","/GameMap/media/learning/core-business-claude.webp","The Core Business mining vehicle in a three-dimensional side-view Mars scene, with fuel, hull, cargo, money and depth indicators.","https://leichtbier.github.io/core-business/",[294],[2218,2219],{"_51":95,"_26":96},{"_51":1078,"_26":1079},[2221],{"_51":1623,"_26":2222,"_207":2223},"https://github.com/Leichtbier/core-business#readme","The author explicitly separates Claude-generated work from ElevenLabs audio and credits Motherload/XGen Studios. This does not imply that Claude created the original game’s rules.",[2225],{"_51":880,"_26":2226,"_207":2227},"https://github.com/Leichtbier/core-business","Complete JavaScript game, vendored Three.js, committed GLBs, Blender source scripts, UI, audio and tests. Serve the root, e.g. python3 -m http.server 5173; Blender regeneration is unnecessary for normal play. Code is MIT with explicit exceptions: ElevenLabs audio is supplied for this project, not separate extraction or redistribution; see LICENSE.",[2229],{"_51":2230,"_26":2215,"_207":2231},"Play Core Business","WebGL browser, keyboard/pointer and touch controls. Initial graphics preparation stalled with the default headless renderer; Chrome with Metal reached normal play. After the opening transmission, brief movement/drilling input produced score 25 and fuel/depth feedback. Full mining progression and audio were not tested.",[2233],{"_51":2234,"_26":2222,"_207":-7},"Read the mining game’s implementation and asset pipeline",[2236,2237,2238,2239],"Start a new game and learn movement, downward drilling, fuel and return-to-surface shops.","Read the fixed-step simulation separately from the Three.js renderer and committed GLB models.","Serve the repository root with a static HTTP server; opening ES modules via file:// does not work.","Change one mineral or upgrade rule, then check drilling, selling, fuel use and save/reload.","The creator attributes the game code, tests, textures, translations, models and Blender generation scripts to Claude Opus 5.5. ElevenLabs supplied the sound and music. The project reimplements Motherload-style rules with new assets and explicitly describes itself as a non-commercial experiment; the coding client is not named.",[1078,2242],"ElevenLabs",[2236,2237,2238,2239],{"_51":2234,"_26":2222,"_18":831},{"_51":2230,"_26":2215,"_18":307,"_207":2231},{"_51":880,"_26":2226,"_259":260,"_207":2227},{"_51":1623,"_26":2222,"_207":2223},[117,1116],[1078,2242],"resource:threejs","resource","A JavaScript 3D rendering library for browsers, with scenes, cameras, materials, and loaders.","/resources/",{"_20":117,"_2318":95,"_246":2319,"_49":2320,"_2317":2252,"_2312":2311,"_26":2274,"_59":2321,"_2295":2322,"_2286":2323,"_2282":2324,"_2279":179},[2257,2258,2259,2260,2261,2262,2263,2264,2265,2266,2267,2268,2269],"website/src/data/resources.json",{"_49":22,"_53":95,"_55":2318,"_57":-7},{"_49":111,"_53":2252,"_55":2317,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":2315,"_53":2316,"_55":246,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":2313,"_53":2314,"_55":49,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_51":2310,"_53":2311,"_55":2312,"_57":58},{"_49":59,"_51":211,"_61":2308,"_55":26,"_57":-7},{"_49":59,"_51":2300,"_61":2301,"_55":59,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_51":2293,"_234":1104,"_61":2294,"_55":2295,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_51":2284,"_234":1104,"_61":2285,"_55":2286,"_57":-7},{"_49":190,"_51":2280,"_234":1104,"_61":2281,"_55":2282,"_57":-7},{"_49":50,"_51":2278,"_53":179,"_55":2279,"_57":90},{"_49":50,"_55":2275,"_51":2276,"_53":2277},{"_49":59,"_55":2270,"_51":2271,"_61":2272},"identitySource","Identity evidence",[2273],{"_51":95,"_26":2274},"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js","identity","Identity & attribution","Official Three.js project/site icon. Do not use mrdoob's personal portrait as an institution logo.","Source reviewed","verified","Tracks",[88,2283],"dimensions","World models","Development stages",[2287,2288,2289,2290,2291,2292],"stages","Planning","Gameplay & code","Assets & animation","Engines & scenes","Testing","Build & release","Topics",[95,2296,2297,2298,2299],"tags","JavaScript","WebGL","WebGPU","Rendering library","Further reading",[2302,2303],{"_51":2306,"_26":2307},{"_51":2304,"_26":2305},"Official examples","https://threejs.org/examples/","Official manual","https://threejs.org/manual/",[2309],{"_51":211,"_26":2274},"Why it belongs here","Lets agents build browser-testable 3D prototypes directly in TypeScript or JavaScript and inspect APIs through source and examples. Game loops, physics, navigation, saves, and other systems need separate design or integration. Validate WebGL and WebGPU paths individually.","detail","Resource type","Tool","Category","Engines & creation tools","summary","name","engines","tool",[2332,2333],[95,2296,2297,2298,2299],[2326,2327,2328,2329,2330,2331],[112,2325],"world","plan","code","assets","scene","test","ship",{"_51":2306,"_26":2307},{"_51":2304,"_26":2305},{"_2335":2336},"documents",{"_2337":2338,"_2339":2340},"en",[2342,2346,2347,2348,2345,2349,2350,2351,2352,2353,2354,2355,2356,2357,2358,2359,2360,2361,2362,2363,2364,2365,2366,2367,2368,2369,2370,2371,2372,2373,2374,2375,2376,2377,2378,2379,2380,2344,2381,2343,2382,2383,2384,2385,2386,2387,2388,2389,2390,2391,2392,2393,2394,2395,2396,2397,2398,2399,2400,2401,2402],"zh",[2341,2342,2343,2344,2345],"reading-guide","practical-guid